{
  "version": 1,
  "_readme": [
    "Hand-authored semantic layer for the KAG graph. This is the ONE manual input, and",
    "its quality caps the whole system's accuracy (plan §13 Q1).",
    "",
    "`column` is the physical BigQuery column a metric is measured by. It is null until",
    "a human confirms it against the real schema. The builder proposes candidates by name",
    "similarity and writes them to backend/data/kag/unmapped.json for review — proposals",
    "are NEVER auto-merged as MEASURED_BY edges. Filling these in is the highest-value",
    "follow-up work: every confirmed mapping removes a chance for the LLM to guess a",
    "column name wrong.",
    "",
    "`aliases` are safe to author without the schema — they are semantics, not physical",
    "facts — and they are what makes 'churn' route to Return Rate % today.",
    "",
    "Two of the four originally-unbacked metrics turned out to be naming variants and",
    "are now mapped to the column that already holds the value:",
    "  Retention Index   -> ris_pct        (RIS *is* the Retention Index Score)",
    "  Performance Index -> overall_score  (the composite in fact_dynamic_scores)",
    "",
    "TWO remain null because the data genuinely does not exist in report_hub_demo:",
    "  Outage Count — fact_network_kpi_points has cqi/rsrp/sinr/score, no outage counter",
    "  Latency      — same table; sinr is signal-to-noise and cqi is channel quality,",
    "                 neither is latency. Mapping either would be a fabrication.",
    "Both were REMOVED from dataSourceMap.ts rather than left advertised: a KPI the model",
    "is told it can use, with no column behind it, is an invitation to invent one. Restore",
    "them there and here together if the columns are ever added upstream."
  ],
